    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0134" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg92"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 455.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> You will learn from the newspapers that
                    General McClernand has attained a very important success in Arkansas. An
                    official despatch from him confirms this information. It is thought that it must
                    result in freeing the west side of the Mississippi from the presence of the
                    insurrectionary forces.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
